    "created_at": "2022-11-29T16:37:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-11-29T16:37:27Z",
    "body": "The reason Safari doesn't match author padding here is because the native appearance can't be painted at certain sizes. One exception is `<button>` where we paint a custom \"native\" style at larger sizes in order to support multi-line/custom content that can be inside buttons, see `data:text/html,<button style=\"padding: 20px\">hello</button><button>world</button>`.\r\n\r\nGiven the Safari _wants_ to render native controls, honoring padding would mean having to support 2 types of \"native\" styling, the styling that's actually native, and one that supports arbitrary sizes. \r\n\r\n@pxlcoder Do you have an opinion regarding this?\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
