    "updated_at": "2022-12-16T00:25:44Z",
    "body": "> Yeah, exactly. This is interopearable in the `<button>` case and not in the `<select>` case (not sure if there are others). I think we should make `<select>` just like `<button>`.\r\n\r\nOk, thanks. Then I agree we should try to make this interoperable. The best option from a developer point of view would seem to be to respect the `padding` even when `appearance:auto`. Chromium-wise, I think that just requires [returning zero here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/layout_theme_default.cc;l=230;drc=d632a0e263747345842d2a01f43179d711c4a5d4) and [something smaller here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/layout/layout_theme_default.cc;l=238;drc=d632a0e263747345842d2a01f43179d711c4a5d4). If we can spec this and get a test, I'm happy to make the Chromium change. This seems hard to write a WPT for, right? I suppose just a `<link rel=\"mismatch\"` type test that makes sure padding has an effect?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
